-- Capability unforgeability (R3), the OVER-BREADTH guard (2026-08-05).
--
-- Accept companion to reject/t143. The rule is "`Cap` may not appear in the
-- solved result type of `from_json`", NOT "`from_json` is suspicious in a
-- module that handles capabilities". This module does both things at once:
-- it narrows a real capability AND decodes an ordinary `Int`.
--
-- The check must read the SOLVED result type and find `Int`. An
-- implementation that keys off the module's `needs`, off the presence of a
-- `Cap` anywhere in scope, or off `from_json` appearing near cap code at all
-- would reject this file.
--
-- Note this file passes today, before the check exists — trivially, since
-- nothing rejects anything yet. That is not the point of it. Its job is to
-- still pass AFTER Check A lands; read it together with reject/t143, because
-- an accept-only witness cannot tell a working contract from one that checks
-- nothing.
mod OrdinaryDecode do
  needs IO

  fn main() do
    let console : Cap(IO.Console) = cap_narrow(root_cap)
    let n : Int = from_json("1")
    println(int_to_string(n))
  end
end
